From bd8597273d544d1ec223182d7ae9af45a5de1481 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Barth <dbarth4@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 16:24:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Replace the regex and bstr uses in codegen_ssa and
 mir_dataflow

Three call sites pulled in the regex engine and bstr, and none of them
needed either:

  - `link.rs` matched linker stderr against
    `(unknown|unrecognized) (command line )?(option|argument)` to decide
    whether to retry the link without a flag the linker rejected.
  - `errors.rs` replaced the first `-[0-9a-f]+` in an rlib name with `-*`,
    and used `bstr::ByteSlice::replace` to write `<sysroot>` over the
    sysroot path, both only to pretty-print a failed link command.
  - `mir_dataflow`'s graphviz dump matched `\t?\u{001f}([+-])` to colour
    the lines of a state diff, behind `-Zdump-mir-dataflow`.

Each is a few lines of byte matching. The replacements are written to be
exactly what the regexes did, including the unanchored match in
`is_unknown_arg_error` and `Regex::replace` stopping at the first hit in
`strip_crate_hash`.

librustc_driver on aarch64-apple-darwin, stripped:
111,360,864 -> 109,442,544, or 1.83 MiB. bstr and aho-corasick leave the
compiler entirely; regex-syntax and regex-automata stay, smaller, because
icu_list and tracing-subscriber's matchers still pull them.
